1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,920
[plane roars overhead]

2
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,340
[birds chirping]

3
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:26,900
Watch closely, now.

4
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:28,820
The size and shape
of the smoke signal

5
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:30,320
relays your message.

6
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,160
-[cloth fluttering]
-[MINE] Come.

7
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:36,700
Run.

8
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:39,080
Help.

9
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,750
-Where are you?
-[exclaims]

10
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:43,340
Enemy.

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,670
[NAGISA] Hey, smoke signals?
What are you thinking?

12
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,260
Put that fire out!

13
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:51,510
What? Why? This is important.

14
00:00:51,630 --> 00:00:53,470
We need to teach Asa
how to communicate

15
00:00:53,590 --> 00:00:55,260
in case we get separated
from her.

16
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:56,600
You'll attract attention!

17
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:58,270
Is this so abnormal?

18
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:00,810
How do people communicate
with each other down here?

19
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:02,440
Over long distances?

20
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,730
[NAGISA] Uh...

21
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:04,940
♪

22
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,230
[NAGISA] We have these things
called "phones."

23
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:10,910
But mine is no use to us.
Even if I could charge it,

24
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:12,860
I bet it won't connect
to the network.

25
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,030
[ASA (CHILD)] Mom, what is this?

26
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,370
Something old.

27
00:01:17,490 --> 00:01:20,250
I had it when I first wandered
into Higashi Village.

28
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:22,710
I looked for a payphone
so I could call for help,

29
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:23,880
but I couldn't find one.

30
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,210
They used to be
on every street corner.

31
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:28,550
I guess the world
got a little less convenient

32
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:30,260
while I was trapped
in the mountains.

33
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,760
Bet my transit card
doesn't work anymore, either.

34
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:37,970
I should still be able to pay
with cash, though. I hope.

35
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:39,970
We need to find the police

36
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,140
or some other form
of protection.

37
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:44,610
But then again,
we haven't put enough distance

38
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:46,230
between us and the village.

39
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,480
Their agents could be
hiding close by,

40
00:01:48,610 --> 00:01:49,860
waiting for us.

41
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:54,070
The village
where my son is still...

42
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:57,870
Mom, Dad, what's the plan?

43
00:01:58,370 --> 00:02:00,370
Aren't we going back
for big brother?

44
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,670
-[NAGISA] Hmm?
-I taught Yuru all that I could.

45
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:05,380
He knows how to survive.

46
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,540
You must have trust
in his abilities.

47
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,170
[Asa (child) gasps]

48
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:13,800
What should we do? We saved Asa,

49
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:16,930
but what if they lock Yuru up
in her cell instead?

50
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:18,140
Huh?

51
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,770
[MAN 1] Hey, someone's here.

52
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,140
I don't recognize them.

53
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:26,520
Kimonos? That's kind of weird.

54
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:28,110
Where are you from?

55
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:30,400
Hi, we're visiting from Tokyo.

56
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:32,900
You caught us
in our cosplaying getups.

57
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:34,240
What's that mean?

58
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,530
Funny story.

59
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,160
We got dressed up
in these period clothes

60
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:39,580
and came out here
to do a photo shoot.

61
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,580
But then we lost our stuff
in the mountains, so--

62
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,200
-Nagisa.
-Huh?

63
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:46,000
Remind me.
Violence isn't allowed here,

64
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:49,090
even if we have
a good reason for it?

65
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,970
[MAN 1] We don't wanna hurt you.
Hand the girl over,

66
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:57,140
and we'll consider
the matter settled.

67
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,680
[MAN 2] You belong
in Higashi Village.

68
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:01,100
Asa's here.

69
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,390
Are you sure fighting
is the only option?

70
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,690
Afraid so.

71
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:07,690
[men grunting]

72
00:03:09,110 --> 00:03:10,940
-[thumping]
-[grunting]

73
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:15,700
[men groaning]

74
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:20,910
[NAGISA] Even if I tried
to find somebody

75
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:23,370
who could take us under
their wing and protect us...

76
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,410
as far as the world's concerned,

77
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:27,500
I've been lost
in the mountains for years.

78
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:30,590
It would be all over the news
if I popped up out of nowhere.

79
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:31,880
People across the globe

80
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,550
would be interested
in our story.

81
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:36,090
We might as well send a map
to Higashi Village

82
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:38,380
telling them exactly
where to find Asa.

83
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:42,010
Where can we go that's safe?

84
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,720
How can we protect
our daughter...

85
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:48,060
and the son
we had to leave behind?

86
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,770
[♪ opening theme song playing]

87
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:08,460
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

88
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:23,410
[SHINGO] Well, damn.

89
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:27,160
The electricity bricked
this stupid piece of crap.

90
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:28,450
[sighs] This is why

91
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:31,790
I try to avoid using Raijin
unless I have to.

92
00:05:32,330 --> 00:05:35,920
Say hello to my daemons,
Fujin and Raijin.

93
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:38,460
Their powers should be obvious.

94
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:42,590
Fujin here controls the wind,
and Raijin controls lightning.

95
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:45,890
-Let's play nice, buddy boy.
-[Yuru grunts]

96
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:48,350
EPISODE 18
FUJIN AND RAIJIN

97
00:05:48,470 --> 00:05:51,390
[MAN 1] Ah, crap.
We lost touch with Shingo!

98
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,060
[MAN 2] Huh? What do you mean?

99
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:54,520
I think that brat they kidnapped

100
00:05:54,650 --> 00:05:56,110
must've done something
to the boss.

101
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:58,520
He said he was going
to crush Shingo's windpipe

102
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:00,530
if we didn't release
the hostages.

103
00:06:00,650 --> 00:06:02,200
It sounded like
somebody was choking,

104
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,570
and then the line went dead.

105
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:06,070
It's no good. My call
won't go through, either.

106
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,620
[grunts] We've got this.

107
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,370
Send some people
to check on him.

108
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,830
Alert the guys
watching the hostages, also!

109
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,120
♪

110
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:16,170
[MAN 1] Huh? What's the issue?

111
00:06:16,290 --> 00:06:17,750
[MAN 2 ON PHONE]
Where are you right now?

112
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,340
[MAN 1] Not far from gate two.

113
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:21,260
[MAN 2] Good.
You're close to Shingo.

114
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,840
Go check on him.
As... as in, now.

115
00:06:23,970 --> 00:06:25,130
We'll be right behind you.

116
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:27,970
Wait, all you want from me
is to go say hi to the boss?

117
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,060
Where's he at?

118
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:34,060
Yeah, okay, that's not far.
I'll head over. Mm.

119
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:35,390
I still don't understand

120
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,310
why this is so important,
though.

121
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,070
That one of Shingo's men?

122
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,520
Sounds like it.

123
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,900
[MAN 1] No way, dude.
The twin brother?

124
00:06:43,030 --> 00:06:45,200
I've heard he's, like,
a feral animal.

125
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,570
What if he gets loose
and comes after me?

126
00:06:48,030 --> 00:06:49,330
Now we're talking.

127
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:51,870
This guy is going to take us
straight to Yuru.

128
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,450
You two ready to show off?

129
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:56,460
[PIGEON-TOES] Yes, yes!
That human doesn't have daemons.

130
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,170
He won't notice us.

131
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:00,210
[MAN 1]
You positive this can't wait?

132
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,590
I just picked up
some dinner and--

133
00:07:01,710 --> 00:07:02,880
[MAN 2] Are you kidding me?

134
00:07:03,010 --> 00:07:05,010
Who do you think paid
for that food, huh?

135
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,220
Right, sorry! I am on my way.

136
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:09,260
-[Bow-Legs grunting]
-[man grunts]

137
00:07:09,390 --> 00:07:11,640
-[Bow-Legs growling]
-[man groaning]

138
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,560
[MAN 2] You there?

139
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:20,690
What was that weird noise?
Hello?

140
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:25,070
It was nothing. My phone
just slipped out of my hand.

141
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:27,110
[PIGEON-TOES]
And just to confirm...

142
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:29,280
Where is Shingo, again?

143
00:07:29,410 --> 00:07:31,450
I don't remember, exactly.

144
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:33,910
[MAN 1] TT Logistics office.

145
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,960
On the second floor.

146
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,580
[PIGEON-TOES]
And could you remind me

147
00:07:37,710 --> 00:07:39,710
where the hostages are, too?

148
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:41,090
[MAN 1] Of course.

149
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:44,960
The hostages are in the
Oedo Transport reception room.

150
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:47,880
Cool. I am out. See you.

151
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:52,100
Nice job. Why don't we go
and grab Yuru first?

152
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:53,350
Yes, sir.

153
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:55,980
Your cute little daemons
are total nightmare fuel.

154
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,520
Who'd have known?

155
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,900
And that means

156
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:03,650
if the twins ever do something
that you don't like,

157
00:08:03,770 --> 00:08:06,530
you can control 'em
with Mamegarasu.

158
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:09,070
Let's worry about that later.

159
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,740
Right now, we should focus
on saving the boy.

160
00:08:11,990 --> 00:08:13,620
[Dera grunts]

161
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,920
Yozakura, is something wrong?

162
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:23,920
[SHINGO] Hm?

163
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:26,420
[scoffs] We've got company.

164
00:08:26,550 --> 00:08:28,340
[Yuru grunts]

165
00:08:29,930 --> 00:08:31,350
[footsteps]

166
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,140
[footsteps continue]

167
00:08:38,270 --> 00:08:39,640
[Yuru breathes shakily]

168
00:08:42,150 --> 00:08:43,520
Hey, good to see you, boss.

169
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:46,320
[Shingo grunts]

170
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,610
-Why are you here?
-[MAN 1] Good question.

171
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:50,860
You weren't answering
your phone, so they sent me here

172
00:08:50,990 --> 00:08:52,490
to make sure
nothing bad happened.

173
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:53,780
The guys were kind of concerned

174
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:55,990
that things weren't going
according to plan.

175
00:08:56,120 --> 00:09:00,080
It looks like they were worried
for nothing...

176
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,960
-[grunts]
-[Bow-Legs chirps]

177
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,130
[YURU] Huh?

178
00:09:05,590 --> 00:09:09,470
[DERA] There's Yuru!
And Asuma Kagemori.

179
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:10,880
Aw, hell. You, too?

180
00:09:11,430 --> 00:09:13,510
[gasps] He's got backup
of his own.

181
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,470
The old guy's daemons
control lightning and wind!

182
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,390
Fujin, go!

183
00:09:19,310 --> 00:09:20,350
[grunting]

184
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,900
[DERA]
That wind slices like a blade.

185
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,860
Raijin, now!

186
00:09:27,270 --> 00:09:28,440
[grunts]

187
00:09:32,570 --> 00:09:33,700
[Yuru gasps]

188
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:36,330
[growls]

189
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:44,380
[grunts] What the...

190
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,000
[Dera gasps]

191
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:47,960
[DERA] He's gone!

192
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,720
Asuma, what did you do?

193
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,130
I took him somewhere safer.

194
00:09:53,430 --> 00:09:55,800
We wouldn't want Yuru
to fall back into enemy hands

195
00:09:55,930 --> 00:09:58,010
when we still have
so much to discuss.

196
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:00,310
This was the wisest option.

197
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:01,810
[Shingo grunts]

198
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:04,690
[DERA] Uh... yeah, so.

199
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:07,400
If Yuru's gone,
then we've got no business here.

200
00:10:07,650 --> 00:10:09,940
[DERA]
Sorry for crashing the party.

201
00:10:10,070 --> 00:10:11,450
[Shingo grunts]

202
00:10:11,570 --> 00:10:12,950
[SHINGO] Fujin.

203
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:14,490
[BOTH] Uh...

204
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,530
-[both grunting]
-[PIGEON-TOES] "Bow-Legs!"

205
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,620
[BOW-LEGS] "Pigeon-Toes!"

206
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:20,750
Are you good down there?

207
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:23,000
Wait! The hell did he go?

208
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,330
[Dera grunts]

209
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:26,750
[BANDIT] Damn it, he's gone.

210
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,880
The bastard's too fast.

211
00:10:29,250 --> 00:10:32,550
[Shingo chuckles]

212
00:10:32,670 --> 00:10:34,470
[grunting]

213
00:10:36,930 --> 00:10:37,930
[running footsteps]

214
00:10:38,390 --> 00:10:40,890
[DERA] The daemon's flying
slower this time.

215
00:10:41,010 --> 00:10:43,600
Good. Easier to tail him.

216
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:45,230
[DERA] Huh?

217
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,570
Do they want me to follow?

218
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,910
[gasps] Whoa-whoa!

219
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:04,000
-[DERA] Yuru, are you okay?
-Good, you made it.

220
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:07,250
Sorry, I got zapped
by the lightning back there.

221
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,840
And I wasn't able
to move until now.

222
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,920
[DERA] So, what's your deal?

223
00:11:12,050 --> 00:11:14,090
Wait, it's okay.
You can put the gun down.

224
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:17,260
This is Yozakura,
Asuma's daemon.

225
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:20,390
They're sort of an ally...
I guess.

226
00:11:20,510 --> 00:11:22,350
-It's complicated.
-[DERA] Huh?

227
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:25,430
[YURU] When they first
kidnapped me, we had a talk,

228
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,690
and they explained
the situation.

229
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,480
What is this? A cloud of moths?

230
00:11:32,610 --> 00:11:33,610
[grunting]

231
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,900
[YOZAKURA] Forgive
the rough treatment, young Yuru.

232
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:37,280
Whoa, it can talk!

233
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,820
[YOZAKURA] If I were to speak,

234
00:11:38,950 --> 00:11:40,870
I would give away
my intelligence.

235
00:11:40,990 --> 00:11:44,250
So instead, I play the part
of the dumb daemon

236
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:47,250
to lower Hayato Shingo's guard.

237
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:48,830
Who's Shingo?

238
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,670
[YOZAKURA] Asuma's uncle.

239
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:53,550
First and foremost,
let me say this.

240
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:56,260
Asuma is no enemy of yours.

241
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,380
Asuma hates Shingo.

242
00:11:58,510 --> 00:12:01,100
He would gladly kill him
if given the chance.

243
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,470
[Yuru grunts]

244
00:12:03,470 --> 00:12:06,140
[YOZAKURA] Gonzo Kagemori
heard of this incident

245
00:12:06,270 --> 00:12:09,810
and is using it both to
weed out traitors in his clan

246
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:11,730
and to deal with Shingo.

247
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:16,070
Asuma leapt at the chance
to take down his uncle.

248
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,490
[YURU] It seems strange

249
00:12:17,610 --> 00:12:19,030
he would want
one of his relations

250
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:20,370
brought down so badly.

251
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:22,200
What's the story with Shingo?

252
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:25,250
[YOZAKURA] It starts
with Asuma's mother, Iori.

253
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:27,790
Shingo never cared
for his little sister.

254
00:12:27,910 --> 00:12:31,130
From the time she was a child,
he treated her as a burden.

255
00:12:31,590 --> 00:12:33,460
But much to his surprise,

256
00:12:33,590 --> 00:12:37,050
the powerful Kagemori head
fell in love with that "burden."

257
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:40,180
It caused quite a stir
in the Shingo clan.

258
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:41,300
[Yuru exhales]

259
00:12:41,430 --> 00:12:43,430
[YOZAKURA] Greedy and grasping,

260
00:12:43,550 --> 00:12:47,060
Hayato used his new in-laws
to expand his wealth.

261
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:48,480
Thanks to his sister,

262
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:51,230
his business
had grown far larger.

263
00:12:51,350 --> 00:12:53,610
Yet still, he chose to deny her,

264
00:12:53,730 --> 00:12:56,480
never even so much
as thanking her.

265
00:12:59,490 --> 00:13:03,070
His avarice knows no bounds.

266
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:05,200
Through the Kagemoris,

267
00:13:05,330 --> 00:13:07,870
he learned of Break and Seal's
existence

268
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,870
and has been making moves
to claim those next.

269
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:14,090
He is like a moth
drawn to a flame.

270
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:18,880
Though, Higashi Village
is no different in that respect.

271
00:13:19,010 --> 00:13:20,510
You want me to say sorry?

272
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:22,800
You're around Shingo
all the time.

273
00:13:22,930 --> 00:13:24,800
Surely you could
lop his head off?

274
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:27,220
Seems like that would've
saved you a lot of trouble.

275
00:13:27,350 --> 00:13:28,810
[YOZAKURA] Hmm.

276
00:13:29,770 --> 00:13:32,310
When facing Fujin and Raijin,

277
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:35,230
Asagiri and I
are severely disadvantaged.

278
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:39,900
Lightning would burn us
and wind would blow us away.

279
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:43,780
We have no recourse
against them.

280
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,740
Asuma is aware of our weakness,

281
00:13:46,870 --> 00:13:49,580
and so feigns obedience
to Shingo.

282
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:54,000
He's a kind boy.
For my sake and Asagiri's,

283
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:56,590
he's had to endure much.

284
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:57,750
[Yuru grunts]

285
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,210
How can you call
that face "kind?"

286
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:03,220
He's got one of the
shadiest smiles I've ever seen.

287
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:04,470
[YOZAKURA] I confess,

288
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:08,810
I don't know how he came
to wear that scheming grin.

289
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:10,730
It does him no favors.

290
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:11,930
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

291
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:14,770
[MAN 1] You're serious?

292
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,900
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

293
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,190
Seems the head
of the Kagemori clan

294
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,190
and Asa showed up.

295
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,440
Huh?

296
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,200
[MAN 1] And it sounds like
no one can get in touch

297
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,610
with the boss anymore.

298
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:27,530
-And what do we make of that?
-[MAN 1] Thing is...

299
00:14:28,330 --> 00:14:29,990
[MAN 2]
The twin brother did what?

300
00:14:30,450 --> 00:14:32,210
[WOMAN] Shingo was captured?

301
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:34,460
[MAN 1] He wants us
to release the kids.

302
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:36,330
[MAN 2] They haven't
found us, right?

303
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,210
[MAN 1] Not as far as we know.

304
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,630
♪

305
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:11,620
[panting]

306
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:20,630
[gasps] My other half is nearby.

307
00:15:20,750 --> 00:15:22,250
[BOTH] That's fantastic.

308
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:24,920
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
Except they're being held

309
00:15:25,050 --> 00:15:26,720
with a girl from the village.

310
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:28,340
She said the guards have daemons

311
00:15:28,470 --> 00:15:29,760
and they don't know
how to escape.

312
00:15:29,890 --> 00:15:31,720
[FEMALE DAEMON] Oh, no.
Are they the ones

313
00:15:31,850 --> 00:15:33,850
-who attacked your village?
-[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Mm-hmm.

314
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,180
It sounds like
they're being used

315
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,270
as bargaining chips for Yuru.

316
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:40,310
[MALE DAEMON] No wonder
we haven't seen her.

317
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,400
Poor thing's trapped over there.

318
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:43,740
One more thing.

319
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:46,150
Apparently, both the twins
are nearby as well.

320
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,530
[BOTH] Yuru and the real Asa?

321
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:50,620
[FEMALE DAEMON]
Then we're in good hands.

322
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,950
We could even ask
the Divine Guardians to help!

323
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,160
[MALE DAEMON] Not to brag,

324
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:55,330
but I think we're pretty
good friends

325
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:56,790
after that first meet-up!

326
00:15:57,870 --> 00:15:59,170
I don't know.

327
00:15:59,290 --> 00:16:01,710
I mean, Asa probably
hates my partner.

328
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:05,590
And would Yuru help...
after what I did to him?

329
00:16:06,130 --> 00:16:09,050
I may have ruined everything
with him for good.

330
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:10,930
[FEMALE DAEMON]
No reason not to check.

331
00:16:11,050 --> 00:16:12,510
[MALE DAEMON]
You missed it after we parted.

332
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:15,640
Yuru said he had questions
he wanted to ask you.

333
00:16:15,770 --> 00:16:16,730
[Danji (tsugai) exhales]

334
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:19,480
[FEMALE DAEMON]
I'm sure he'll come,

335
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,190
even if he's mad.

336
00:16:21,310 --> 00:16:24,070
Maybe, but how are we supposed
to contact him

337
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:25,900
without all the bad guys
finding us?

338
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:26,950
♪

339
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:28,900
We can't really hide.

340
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:31,570
This place is teeming
with daemons.

341
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:33,490
Who knows if any of them
are friendly?

342
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:35,120
We'd be safe
with Left and Right,

343
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:38,000
but I've got no idea
where they might be.

344
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,710
[daemons sigh]

345
00:16:39,830 --> 00:16:41,130
[sighs]

346
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,250
[gasps]

347
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:49,880
[YOZAKURA] I must apologize.

348
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:53,300
I put you both through
quite a bit before explaining.

349
00:16:53,430 --> 00:16:54,760
You got that right.

350
00:16:54,890 --> 00:16:57,350
I still don't see why you had
to leave us in the dark.

351
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:59,350
Not like we wouldn't
have helped you.

352
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:01,940
Seems like it's in
our best interests as well.

353
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:04,020
[YOZAKURA] If I had said
everything earlier,

354
00:17:04,150 --> 00:17:05,900
Shingo would've caught on.

355
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:09,240
I've limited communication
to protect Asuma,

356
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:10,740
as he's done for us.

357
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:12,030
Oh, yeah.

358
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:15,200
Jin hinted at this
when we had our little chat.

359
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:17,080
[JIN] I'm caught up now.

360
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,660
The enemy knows
that Yuru is off the mountain

361
00:17:19,790 --> 00:17:21,370
and is trying to get him alone.

362
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,630
Furthermore,
they sent a Daemon Wielder

363
00:17:23,750 --> 00:17:25,500
to Higashi Village
who was strong enough

364
00:17:25,630 --> 00:17:28,260
to kidnap the fake Asa
and one of the children.

365
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,550
We need someone
who matches Shingo's greed

366
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:32,720
and has a whole slew of daemons?

367
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,300
-Funny.
-Sounds familiar.

368
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:37,310
Yeah, we've got a guy.

369
00:17:37,430 --> 00:17:39,470
Besides, we were planning
on crushing them,

370
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,680
so this all works out.

371
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:41,940
[Dera chuckles]

372
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:44,310
[JIN] On the day of the meeting,
we'll send them.

373
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,320
You can go now, Tadera.

374
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,530
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

375
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:49,570
We're not gonna try
fleshin' out a plan

376
00:17:49,690 --> 00:17:51,070
or anything more detailed?

377
00:17:51,190 --> 00:17:52,700
The longer we stay
chatting here,

378
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,780
the more likely
someone takes notice.

379
00:17:54,910 --> 00:17:57,240
We can improvise the rest
on the spot.

380
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,700
How reassuring.

381
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,790
[JIN] One more thing.

382
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:04,630
While you're there,
you're likely to run into Asuma.

383
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,460
Pretend like
you're out to get him.

384
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:08,760
He's not actually
on the enemy's side,

385
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,960
so please refrain
from attacking.

386
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:15,050
And take these.
It's some photos from Asa.

387
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:18,720
On her behalf, give them
to Mr. Big Brother.

388
00:18:18,850 --> 00:18:20,640
And that was the whole meeting.

389
00:18:20,770 --> 00:18:23,310
-There's no plan?
-Like you're one to talk.

390
00:18:23,430 --> 00:18:26,440
[YOZAKURA] Shingo has
recently hired a Daemon Wielder

391
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,400
of masterful skill.

392
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:31,400
We're being particularly
cautious of late

393
00:18:31,530 --> 00:18:33,150
to avoid his notice.

394
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,070
He wields dual katanas,

395
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:38,120
one long, one short. Be careful.

396
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:40,870
I know him, the sword pervert.

397
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:42,120
[YOZAKURA] Ivan Yosano.

398
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:43,410
Say what now?

399
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:45,920
[DERA] He was seen on the prowl
at night after women.

400
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:50,250
[grunts] Then he deserves to die
a thousand times over!

401
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:52,050
He should disembowel himself!

402
00:18:52,170 --> 00:18:53,470
[DERA] I'm afraid
a crime like that

403
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:54,800
doesn't get you
the death penalty

404
00:18:54,930 --> 00:18:56,090
in modern-day Japan.

405
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:58,350
-About this perv--
-[YOZAKURA] Ivan.

406
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:01,560
[grunts] I may or may not have
seen him come to blows

407
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,020
with Left and Right.

408
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:04,430
And he may or may not know

409
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,890
something about
your mom and dad.

410
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,270
[Yuru gasps softly]

411
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:10,400
[DERA] I didn't like how dodgy
he was about it.

412
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:14,610
I'll bet they're still fighting.

413
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:17,990
They said they'll bring him
back to you alive.

414
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,290
[YURU] Got it.

415
00:19:22,410 --> 00:19:24,960
Then that means we need
to help them. Let's go.

416
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:27,130
Sure. Just let me grab my rifle.

417
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:29,380
Hey, Yozakura,
I don't suppose you could--

418
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,300
[YOZAKURA]
I obey only Asuma's orders.

419
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:34,170
[DERA] Yeah, of course.

420
00:19:34,510 --> 00:19:35,970
♪

421
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:40,470
[YURU] Smoke signals.

422
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:41,810
[DERA] What?

423
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:44,180
Over there. You see?

424
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:46,890
Maybe? Hmm.

425
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:48,520
Just seems like fire.

426
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:50,440
No way. I know those.

427
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:52,570
I learned them
back in the village.

428
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:54,150
When I went to hunt,

429
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:56,650
Danji and I would use them
to talk.

430
00:19:57,820 --> 00:20:00,320
"Need help."

431
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:02,580
[grunts]

432
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:05,240
Danji's asking us to help him.

433
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:09,000
Before, he said he'd look
for his other half.

434
00:20:09,130 --> 00:20:12,000
So if he really found her...

435
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:14,250
Gotta make a choice.

436
00:20:16,210 --> 00:20:20,140
The hostages,
or the lead on your parents?

437
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:24,220
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
I asked Yuru for help.

438
00:20:24,350 --> 00:20:25,720
[ASA (FAKE)] Big brother?

439
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:27,100
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
There's no way to be sure

440
00:20:27,230 --> 00:20:29,060
he'll see the smoke signals.

441
00:20:29,190 --> 00:20:31,730
[ASA (FAKE)] Even if he does,
would he help us?

442
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:33,940
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] I don't know.

443
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:37,400
I mean, we did
something terrible to him.

444
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:39,200
[Azami cries]

445
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:41,450
[ASA (FAKE)]
Azami, it'll be okay.

446
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:45,200
Someone's on their way
to save us right now.

447
00:20:45,330 --> 00:20:47,790
-Who is it?
-My brother.

448
00:20:48,540 --> 00:20:51,540
I know him, and there's no way
he'd ever abandon you.

449
00:20:51,670 --> 00:20:54,090
[gasps] Yuru is coming?

450
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:56,460
[sighs]

451
00:20:56,590 --> 00:20:57,960
♪

452
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,090
If we don't hear anything...

453
00:21:01,470 --> 00:21:03,510
[ASA (FAKE)] I just hope
he's careful coming here.

454
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,100
These people are tough,

455
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:06,770
and they all have daemons.

456
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,430
This really sucks.

457
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:09,980
[MAN] What? You're here?

458
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:12,020
-[crashing]
-[all grunt]

459
00:21:13,770 --> 00:21:15,110
[all grunt]

460
00:21:21,650 --> 00:21:23,200
[whimpering]

461
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,620
[yelling]

462
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:31,160
-You really came!
-Yuru!

463
00:21:31,620 --> 00:21:35,380
[ASA] I wasn't expecting to see
a Higashi Village smoke signal.

464
00:21:36,130 --> 00:21:39,130
The world below has given up
the practice altogether.

465
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:42,760
So I thought I'd find
my brother here.

466
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:45,050
[grunts]

467
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:47,350
GALAXY'S LOUDEST TONGUE CLICK

468
00:21:47,470 --> 00:21:50,430
-[both trembling]
-[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Sorry.

469
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:53,770
The scary twin showed up.

470
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

471
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:27,910
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

472
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:29,410
[ASA] Grab those two.

473
00:23:29,830 --> 00:23:32,080
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Why wouldn't
you go to them before me?

474
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,910
[YURU] Which arm did you use
to cut down my parents?

475
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:38,040
The next shot I fire
goes into that one!

476
00:23:38,170 --> 00:23:39,960
EPISODE 19
SWORD AND BOW
